{
 "about": "Shared cases for the canonical id scheme reg://federal/{corpus}/{collection}/{unit}[#paragraph] (DM-101, SEC-101). The Python module (reader/app/ids.py) and its future TypeScript twin must both pass every case. valid: an address and everything derived from it. citations: a citation string and the address it resolves to. store_keys: a store row's own key and its address. invalid_ids: strings the id parser must refuse. hostile: inputs the resolver must refuse, whatever their type. generated: prefix + fill x count + suffix, which must be refused quickly. destinations: what the safe-destination check accepts and rejects.",
